WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.447 position:50% size:92% align:center
On this teaching model, the SM’s shared memory

00:00:03.447 --> 00:00:06.295 position:50% size:92% align:center
has thirty-two banks, and successive four-byte

00:00:06.295 --> 00:00:08.152 position:50% size:92% align:center
words select successive banks.

00:00:08.372 --> 00:00:11.156 position:50% size:92% align:center
For a word index, taking the remainder after

00:00:11.156 --> 00:00:13.876 position:50% size:92% align:center
division by thirty-two identifies its bank.

00:00:15.896 --> 00:00:19.016 position:50% size:92% align:center
With stride thirty-two, lane zero requests word

00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:21.340 position:50% size:92% align:center
zero, lane one word thirty-two, and

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.000 position:50% size:92% align:center
lane two word sixty-four.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.949 position:50% size:92% align:center
Those are different addresses,

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:26.505 position:50% size:92% align:center
but each maps to bank zero.

00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:31.460 position:50% size:92% align:center
Across the warp, bank zero receives thirty-two

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.949 position:50% size:92% align:center
distinct-word requests. The model needs

00:00:33.949 --> 00:00:35.608 position:50% size:92% align:center
thirty-two service rounds.

00:00:35.828 --> 00:00:38.931 position:50% size:92% align:center
Shared memory is on the SM, but being local does

00:00:38.931 --> 00:00:40.871 position:50% size:92% align:center
not make every address pattern

00:00:40.871 --> 00:00:42.164 position:50% size:92% align:center
equally serviceable.

00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:47.042 position:50% size:92% align:center
Stride thirty-three changes the bank remainder

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:49.713 position:50% size:92% align:center
for successive lanes. This warp’s words now

00:00:49.713 --> 00:00:51.267 position:50% size:92% align:center
use all thirty-two banks.

00:00:51.487 --> 00:00:53.332 position:50% size:92% align:center
The model can serve the distinct

00:00:53.332 --> 00:00:54.601 position:50% size:92% align:center
requests in one round.

00:00:56.621 --> 00:00:59.653 position:50% size:92% align:center
Consider a third case: every lane requests word

00:00:59.653 --> 00:01:02.104 position:50% size:92% align:center
zero. They all select bank zero again.

00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:05.175 position:50% size:92% align:center
Pause and predict whether that necessarily means

00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:07.551 position:50% size:92% align:center
thirty-two distinct-word service rounds.

00:01:13.371 --> 00:01:16.025 position:50% size:92% align:center
There is only one distinct word to supply, so

00:01:16.025 --> 00:01:17.558 position:50% size:92% align:center
the model broadcasts it to

00:01:17.558 --> 00:01:19.033 position:50% size:92% align:center
the readers in one round.

00:01:19.253 --> 00:01:21.998 position:50% size:92% align:center
Count distinct words within each bank. The

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:24.417 position:50% size:92% align:center
starter’s reported service rounds are

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.359 position:50% size:92% align:center
address-model results, not measured GPU time.
